# FCE vocabulary memes — Comic mode rollout

When adding **Comic** retell strips for a meme pack (lifestyle, clothes, future units):

## Data (mandatory)

1. **`js/unitN-<topic>-meme-comics.js`** — array `UNITN_<TOPIC>_MEME_COMICS`:
   - One object per **part** (`part: 1…`, `hero`, `title`, `panels[]`).
   - **Every flip-card** in `unitN-<topic>-meme-cards.js` for that part must appear **once**, same order as cards.
   - `panels[].cardId` matches `cards[].id`; `caption` = book line (verbatim from cards / retell blocks / transcript).
2. Do **not** skip cards that share the same sentence — each image is its own panel.

## Wiring

| Surface | What to add |
|--------|-------------|
| `unitN-vocabulary/<topic>/memes/index.html` | `fce-vocab-meme-comic.css`, `fce-vocab-meme-comic-engine.js`, comics data script, `fce-vocab-meme-parts-engine.js` v2+, pass `comics:` to `FCE_VOCAB_MEME_PARTS.mount` |
| `js/fce-unit-memes-bridge.js` | `comics: (W.UNITN_…_MEME_COMICS \|\| []).slice()` on the parts deck |
| `unitN-lexical-games.html` | Same CSS + comics script if embed uses parts + comic |

## UX (shared engine + CSS)

- Reuse **`FCE_VOCAB_MEME_COMIC.mount`** + **`FCE_VOCAB_MEME_PARTS`** Flip | Comic tabs — no one-off comic UI.
- Images: **WebP** paths in card data when available; `object-fit: contain` — never crop.
- Full-width comic shell: `body.meme-parts-compact.meme-view-comic main.page.meme-parts-shell` with `!important` over `mastering-b2-page-skin.css`.
- **Hide text · retell from memory** toggle stays in comic toolbar.

## Grid layout (`css/fce-vocab-meme-comic.css`)

Desktop default: **3 columns**.

| Panel count | Layout |
|-------------|--------|
| **4–6** | **2 columns** (larger images — Ben, short speakers) |
| **5** | 2×2 + last panel centred on row 3 |
| **7** | 3+3+1 centred |
| **10** | 3+3+3+1 centred |
| **11** | 6-col subgrid, last row pair centred |
| Mobile ≤640px | 2 columns |

Bump `?v=` on comic CSS when changing layout.

